quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  5,77,"Say: ‘O People of the Book! Do not exaggerate in your religion beyond the truth, and do not follow the low desires of a people who went astray before and led many astray, and (now again after the raising of Prophet Muhammad (blessings and peace be upon him) have strayed from the right path.’"
  5,78,"The disbelievers among the Children of Israel were cursed by the tongue of Dawud (David) and ‘Isa, son of Maryam (Jesus, son of Mary). That was because they disobeyed and used to transgress."
  5,79,"They would not forbid one another from the wrong they committed. Surely, evil is what they had been doing."
  5,80,"You see many of them allying themselves with the disbelievers. Indeed, evil is what they have forwarded to their account. Since Allah has become angry with them, they shall remain in everlasting punishment!"
  5,81,"Had they believed in Allah, the Prophet (blessings and peace be upon him), and what was revealed to him, they would never have taken those (pagans) for allies. But most of them are disobedient."
  5,82,You will surely find the most hostile of all people towards the believers to be the Jews and the polytheists. And you will surely find the nearest of them in affection to the believers to be those who say: ‘We are Christians.’ That is because among them are priests and monks and because they are not arrogant.
